1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:04,045
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,302 --> 00:00:15,432
[Ivy] <i>I want to be part</i>
<i>of Ardiente's progress.</i>

3
00:00:15,515 --> 00:00:20,562
<i>I will support Congressman Julio Ardiente</i>

4
00:00:20,645 --> 00:00:22,731
<i>in his bid for the Senate.</i>

5
00:00:22,814 --> 00:00:26,818
<i>Just a piece of advice, Julio.</i>
<i>Be careful in dealing with her.</i>

6
00:00:26,901 --> 00:00:28,820
<i>There's something about that woman.</i>

7
00:00:28,903 --> 00:00:31,322
<i>Don't worry. I know what I'm doing.</i>

8
00:00:31,406 --> 00:00:34,576
<i>I'm Julio Ardiente.</i>
<i>And I don't make mistakes.</i>

9
00:00:35,994 --> 00:00:39,205
[Arnaldo] <i>Thank you for investing</i>
<i>in our project, by the way.</i>

10
00:00:39,289 --> 00:00:42,584
[Ivy] <i>I don't need your thanks.</i>
<i>I invested a lot.</i>

11
00:00:42,667 --> 00:00:46,337
<i>That means, Mr. Mayor,</i>
<i>I'll expect a lot in return.</i>

12
00:00:46,421 --> 00:00:48,757
<i>My boyfriend is not a book.</i>

13
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:50,341
<i>Nor is he a toy</i>

14
00:00:50,425 --> 00:00:52,010
<i>that can be borrowed or shared.</i>

15
00:00:52,093 --> 00:00:53,845
<i>My boyfriend? He's mine.</i>

16
00:00:53,928 --> 00:00:57,932
[Ivy] <i>You can have Arnaldo.</i>
<i>I don't like secondhand things.</i>

17
00:00:58,016 --> 00:01:00,477
<i>I like my toys brand new.</i>

18
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:04,272
<i>How will you benefit</i>
<i>from investing in Ardiente?</i>

19
00:01:04,355 --> 00:01:05,940
<i>Never mind. I already know the answer.</i>

20
00:01:06,024 --> 00:01:08,401
[Emilia] <i>Use your head.</i>
<i>You're so stupid!</i>

21
00:01:08,485 --> 00:01:09,486
-[Diego] <i>Mom.</i>
<i>-That's enough, Governor.</i>

22
00:01:09,569 --> 00:01:14,949
<i>I'd never entrust my life</i>
<i>to anyone I think is stupid.</i>

23
00:01:15,492 --> 00:01:18,286
<i>I'm sorry, but you may leave.</i>

24
00:01:18,369 --> 00:01:20,622
[Carlotta] <i>Calm down.</i>

25
00:01:20,705 --> 00:01:23,875
<i>All that anger won't do you any good.</i>

26
00:01:24,918 --> 00:01:28,838
<i>Jepoy, what did they do to my mother?</i>

27
00:01:28,922 --> 00:01:31,382
[Ivy wailing]

28
00:01:33,468 --> 00:01:34,636
[knocking on door]

29
00:01:36,179 --> 00:01:37,555
Come in.

30
00:01:46,815 --> 00:01:47,857
Grandpa.

31
00:01:53,113 --> 00:01:54,823
You're giving me tea?

32
00:01:56,324 --> 00:01:59,160
Do I look weak to you?

33
00:01:59,244 --> 00:02:01,329
Grandpa, you're not getting any younger.

34
00:02:01,412 --> 00:02:04,374
Tea is better for you than alcohol.

35
00:02:04,457 --> 00:02:06,960
Don't waste my time, boy.

36
00:02:08,878 --> 00:02:09,921
What do you need?

37
00:02:11,131 --> 00:02:13,341
I'm just worried about the farmers.

38
00:02:14,217 --> 00:02:17,053
Grandpa, they worked on that land
their entire lives.

39
00:02:17,137 --> 00:02:19,722
We can't just force them to leave.

40
00:02:19,806 --> 00:02:22,684
I can do whatever I want

41
00:02:22,767 --> 00:02:24,811
and they can't do anything about it.

42
00:02:24,894 --> 00:02:27,188
My project there will push through.

43
00:02:28,064 --> 00:02:28,898
But Grandpa,

44
00:02:28,982 --> 00:02:33,653
you promised you'd give them that land
during the last elections.

45
00:02:33,736 --> 00:02:35,989
Aren't you going to keep your word?

46
00:02:36,072 --> 00:02:37,532
Are you telling me what to do?

47
00:02:37,615 --> 00:02:38,992
[tense music playing]

48
00:02:39,075 --> 00:02:40,160
It's not like that.

49
00:02:40,910 --> 00:02:43,872
I'm just reminding you in case you forgot.

50
00:02:43,955 --> 00:02:48,877
Drinking alcohol every night
could affect a person's memory.

51
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:50,169
Shut up, Diego.

52
00:02:51,504 --> 00:02:57,510
How many times do I have to
remind you that your farmers

53
00:02:57,594 --> 00:03:01,180
are just like worker ants?

54
00:03:02,223 --> 00:03:06,978
Their role in life
is to simply serve those above them.

55
00:03:08,354 --> 00:03:09,230
That's us.

56
00:03:12,150 --> 00:03:14,736
You may have lost weight
and gained muscle,

57
00:03:16,279 --> 00:03:18,031
but your brain has dried up.

58
00:03:18,114 --> 00:03:19,782
No, it hasn't.

59
00:03:21,618 --> 00:03:23,745
I just see things clearer now.

60
00:03:25,079 --> 00:03:27,790
You studied
community development.

61
00:03:29,334 --> 00:03:30,710
Is that
what you're so proud of?

62
00:03:32,295 --> 00:03:36,257
They shouldn't have let you
study in that university

63
00:03:36,341 --> 00:03:38,468
filled with activists.

64
00:03:40,929 --> 00:03:42,555
You may leave, Diego.

65
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:44,682
I'll leave,

66
00:03:45,391 --> 00:03:49,604
but this won't be the last time I fight
for the people of this town.

67
00:03:53,024 --> 00:03:54,651
You should rest, Grandpa.

68
00:03:57,278 --> 00:03:58,404
Thanks for the tea, by the way.

69
00:04:07,038 --> 00:04:08,039
Dad?

70
00:04:08,581 --> 00:04:10,083
-Yeah?
-Where are you going?

71
00:04:10,708 --> 00:04:12,168
I just have to do something real quick.

72
00:04:13,795 --> 00:04:15,129
Go to bed.

73
00:04:16,756 --> 00:04:18,007
Maybe in a while.

74
00:04:18,716 --> 00:04:19,634
What is it?

75
00:04:19,717 --> 00:04:21,302
[sighs]

76
00:04:22,804 --> 00:04:24,222
I spoke to Grandpa.

77
00:04:25,265 --> 00:04:26,266
[scoffs]

78
00:04:26,849 --> 00:04:29,727
You know what, son? I'll be frank.

79
00:04:31,229 --> 00:04:34,357
If this is about those farmers
you want to help,

80
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:37,902
just drop it because you will never change
your grandfather's decision.

81
00:04:38,486 --> 00:04:42,282
But Dad, I just want to fight
for their rights.

82
00:04:42,365 --> 00:04:44,075
But you won't win.

83
00:04:44,158 --> 00:04:46,911
Because no matter what you do
for the people here,

84
00:04:46,995 --> 00:04:48,955
you can't change their lives.

85
00:04:49,956 --> 00:04:55,753
As long as this family
is in power, nothing will change.

86
00:04:57,088 --> 00:04:58,589
Just accept that, son.

87
00:04:58,673 --> 00:05:01,092
[light piano music playing]

88
00:05:04,512 --> 00:05:07,015
If you can stay away from trouble, do it.

89
00:05:08,433 --> 00:05:11,144
I don't want anything bad
happening to you.

90
00:05:15,732 --> 00:05:17,025
I have to go.

91
00:05:21,070 --> 00:05:22,363
Take care, Dad.

92
00:05:22,447 --> 00:05:25,241
[instrumental theme music playing]

93
00:05:27,368 --> 00:05:28,911
[shoveling sound]

94
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:57,065
[sobbing]

95
00:06:05,073 --> 00:06:06,741
You know, Mom?

96
00:06:11,621 --> 00:06:14,082
Every day, I ask myself…

97
00:06:17,585 --> 00:06:20,046
why this happened to us.

98
00:06:23,549 --> 00:06:27,095
Why did this happen to our family?

99
00:06:29,263 --> 00:06:31,432
<i>Why us, Mom? Why us?</i>

100
00:06:34,477 --> 00:06:36,479
<i>Why did this happen to us?</i>

101
00:06:37,146 --> 00:06:40,900
[instrumental theme music playing]

102
00:06:42,401 --> 00:06:45,863
I feel nothing but…

103
00:06:48,574 --> 00:06:49,909
pain…

104
00:06:52,036 --> 00:06:53,412
anger…

105
00:06:55,414 --> 00:06:56,457
and fury.

106
00:06:59,669 --> 00:07:02,547
That's what I feel when I think
about the people

107
00:07:02,630 --> 00:07:04,632
who did this to you.

108
00:07:05,174 --> 00:07:07,552
[ominous music playing]

109
00:07:10,054 --> 00:07:11,931
I'm furious, Mom.

110
00:07:17,019 --> 00:07:19,689
I promise you and Dad…

111
00:07:21,816 --> 00:07:24,318
I'll avenge your deaths.

112
00:07:24,986 --> 00:07:27,488
I will avenge you both.

113
00:07:28,739 --> 00:07:30,700
[tense music playing]

114
00:07:42,003 --> 00:07:43,713
Ivy?

115
00:07:43,796 --> 00:07:45,840
Ivy, wait! Ivy!

116
00:07:45,923 --> 00:07:47,425
Ivy!

117
00:07:50,261 --> 00:07:53,264
[tense music playing]

118
00:07:54,974 --> 00:07:57,351
[Raul] <i>No matter what you do</i>
<i>for the people here,</i>

119
00:07:57,435 --> 00:07:59,145
<i>you can't change their lives.</i>

120
00:07:59,228 --> 00:08:03,774
<i>As long as this family is in power,</i>
<i>nothing will change.</i>

121
00:08:03,858 --> 00:08:05,151
<i>Just accept that, son.</i>

122
00:08:06,027 --> 00:08:09,155
I still believe there's hope
for this town.

123
00:08:11,949 --> 00:08:13,826
If I was able to change for the better…

124
00:08:15,703 --> 00:08:18,122
then I can change this whole place too.

125
00:08:38,184 --> 00:08:41,395
[dramatic music playing]

126
00:09:05,002 --> 00:09:08,005
<i>Someday, I'll change all of Ardiente.</i>

127
00:09:08,756 --> 00:09:11,133
<i>And my family too.</i>

128
00:09:14,512 --> 00:09:17,515
[brooding music playing]

129
00:09:39,912 --> 00:09:41,872
LONG LIVE!
CONGRESSMAN JULIO ARDIENTE

130
00:09:41,956 --> 00:09:44,208
[Emilia] <i>Maids like you</i>
<i>should have presence of mind.</i>

131
00:09:44,292 --> 00:09:46,377
<i>Use your head.</i>
<i>You're so stupid!</i>

132
00:09:46,460 --> 00:09:51,841
<i>Can you further extend</i>
<i>your assistance to Poblacion Ardiente?</i>

133
00:09:51,924 --> 00:09:56,762
[Pablo] <i>Be careful around Julio.</i>
<i>He's clever, like you.</i>

134
00:09:58,889 --> 00:10:01,892
[brooding music playing]

135
00:10:08,232 --> 00:10:10,735
[Emilia] <i>Didn't you start all this?</i>

136
00:10:10,818 --> 00:10:13,195
<i>If only you didn't take a liking</i>
<i>to that girl's mother,</i>

137
00:10:13,279 --> 00:10:15,948
<i>her father wouldn't have gone against us!</i>

138
00:10:16,032 --> 00:10:19,035
[Raul] <i>You enjoyed murdering those people.</i>

139
00:10:19,118 --> 00:10:20,661
<i>You wiped out an entire family!</i>

140
00:10:20,745 --> 00:10:24,290
[Ivy] How could they do this to her?

141
00:10:24,373 --> 00:10:26,959
[Ivy wailing]

142
00:10:27,043 --> 00:10:29,295
Mom!

143
00:10:38,804 --> 00:10:41,807
[tense music playing]

144
00:11:11,087 --> 00:11:15,549
[Julio] <i>As long as this statue</i>
<i>stands firm in our town,</i>

145
00:11:15,633 --> 00:11:19,970
<i>you will continue to have</i>
<i>honest service and leadership</i>

146
00:11:20,054 --> 00:11:24,517
<i>as promised by</i>
<i>your very own Governor Julio!</i>

147
00:11:30,564 --> 00:11:32,650
[tense music playing]

148
00:12:15,901 --> 00:12:17,278
[screaming]

149
00:12:18,028 --> 00:12:19,238
[banging]

150
00:12:23,367 --> 00:12:24,994
Crook!

151
00:12:26,704 --> 00:12:29,623
You bastard! You monster!

152
00:12:30,749 --> 00:12:34,920
You monster! You killed my parents!

153
00:12:37,006 --> 00:12:41,760
You killed my parents! You're monsters!

154
00:12:44,513 --> 00:12:46,223
[shouting] You monsters!

155
00:12:49,643 --> 00:12:51,687
[sobbing] You're all monsters!

156
00:12:51,770 --> 00:12:54,648
You monsters.

157
00:12:54,732 --> 00:12:57,651
I'll kill you all.

158
00:12:57,735 --> 00:13:01,614
I'll kill all of you Ardientes!

159
00:13:03,365 --> 00:13:05,409
[shouting] Ardientes!

160
00:13:06,869 --> 00:13:09,788
[shouting] You monsters!

161
00:13:11,957 --> 00:13:13,959
Ivy! Ivy!

162
00:13:14,043 --> 00:13:16,086
[Ivy wailing]

163
00:13:19,882 --> 00:13:23,052
-I'll kill them all!
-What did you do?

164
00:13:25,721 --> 00:13:27,389
They're monsters.

165
00:13:27,473 --> 00:13:31,227
We have to go now. Ivy.

166
00:13:34,396 --> 00:13:36,273
Come on.

167
00:13:36,357 --> 00:13:38,734
[Ivy crying]

168
00:13:38,817 --> 00:13:40,486
Hold on.

169
00:13:41,028 --> 00:13:43,030
They're monsters.

170
00:13:45,282 --> 00:13:48,661
[gentle music playing]

171
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:04,885
[dramatic music playing]

172
00:14:13,811 --> 00:14:16,689
NEW ARDIENTE

173
00:14:20,276 --> 00:14:21,402
[Diego] Good morning!

174
00:14:21,485 --> 00:14:22,611
-[Pandoy] Diego!
-[Loring] What--

175
00:14:22,695 --> 00:14:23,654
Do you like it?

176
00:14:24,238 --> 00:14:25,990
It's nice.

177
00:14:26,073 --> 00:14:27,783
[Pandoy] Oh? Oh!

178
00:14:27,867 --> 00:14:29,368
"New Ardiente"?

179
00:14:29,451 --> 00:14:32,872
Can we still have that?

180
00:14:32,955 --> 00:14:36,000
Is change still possible in this place?

181
00:14:36,584 --> 00:14:37,877
Of course, Uncle!

182
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:39,837
Like they say, everything changes.

183
00:14:40,421 --> 00:14:42,631
The only constant thing
is the speed of light.

184
00:14:42,715 --> 00:14:43,924
What?

185
00:14:44,508 --> 00:14:47,136
What Diego meant was,

186
00:14:47,219 --> 00:14:49,513
"When there's life, there's hope."

187
00:14:49,597 --> 00:14:51,265
You're right, Auntie.

188
00:14:51,348 --> 00:14:53,392
-I told you so!
-Okay.

189
00:14:53,475 --> 00:14:55,895
How was the party last night?

190
00:14:57,688 --> 00:14:58,898
It was awful.

191
00:14:59,607 --> 00:15:03,027
Grandpa announced that
their project here will push through.

192
00:15:03,110 --> 00:15:05,571
What? That fast?

193
00:15:06,155 --> 00:15:10,034
They got more than enough funds
from the huge amount

194
00:15:10,117 --> 00:15:11,744
Ivy Aguas invested.

195
00:15:12,620 --> 00:15:14,914
Some rich people are unbelievable.

196
00:15:14,997 --> 00:15:18,125
All they think about is earning money.

197
00:15:18,208 --> 00:15:20,836
She should just leave our town.

198
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:23,047
As long as she's here,

199
00:15:23,130 --> 00:15:25,966
it'll be difficult
to change my family's mind.

200
00:15:26,050 --> 00:15:27,968
Their greed for money is getting worse!

201
00:15:29,136 --> 00:15:30,763
What are we going to do, then?

202
00:15:31,513 --> 00:15:33,974
Your grandfather's project
has to be stopped.

203
00:15:34,058 --> 00:15:37,144
[tense music]

204
00:15:37,227 --> 00:15:38,896
NEW ARDIENTE

205
00:15:42,483 --> 00:15:45,486
[instrumental theme music playing]

206
00:15:53,410 --> 00:15:56,455
Ivy, you're awake.

207
00:15:56,538 --> 00:16:00,584
Here. I brought you breakfast.

208
00:16:04,338 --> 00:16:05,923
How are you?

209
00:16:06,548 --> 00:16:08,050
I'm fine.

210
00:16:10,761 --> 00:16:13,973
Ivy, I'm worried about you.

211
00:16:15,391 --> 00:16:18,060
You might get in trouble for what you did.

212
00:16:20,813 --> 00:16:21,981
Nanny.

213
00:16:23,065 --> 00:16:23,899
I won't.

214
00:16:25,317 --> 00:16:28,570
I'm sure Jepoy will do his job.

215
00:16:32,241 --> 00:16:33,367
[sighs deeply]

216
00:16:35,244 --> 00:16:37,287
It felt so good, Nanny.

217
00:16:38,038 --> 00:16:41,041
When I managed to…

218
00:16:42,918 --> 00:16:44,503
wreck…

219
00:16:45,963 --> 00:16:47,464
smash…

220
00:16:49,299 --> 00:16:52,720
and destroy
the Ardientes' symbol of power.

221
00:16:52,803 --> 00:16:54,513
It felt amazing.

222
00:16:54,596 --> 00:16:56,890
Ivy. Take it easy.

223
00:16:57,725 --> 00:17:01,520
Don't let your anger consume you.

224
00:17:01,603 --> 00:17:02,771
Hmm?

225
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:05,899
I won't let that happen.

226
00:17:07,484 --> 00:17:09,069
Here,

227
00:17:09,945 --> 00:17:12,656
now, I am Ivy Aguas.

228
00:17:13,699 --> 00:17:18,996
I'll use this identity
to grip the Ardientes

229
00:17:19,079 --> 00:17:20,414
in the palm of my hand.

230
00:17:21,248 --> 00:17:25,294
This is Ivy, not Lily. This isn't Lily.

231
00:17:26,879 --> 00:17:28,213
Now…

232
00:17:30,340 --> 00:17:33,218
I'll work on completely
winning Emilia's trust.

233
00:17:35,429 --> 00:17:36,472
That's my current goal.

234
00:17:39,641 --> 00:17:44,063
-Nanny, don't worry.
-Okay.

235
00:17:49,068 --> 00:17:53,280
[woman] Rice cakes! Rice cakes!

236
00:17:53,363 --> 00:17:55,866
[tense music playing]

237
00:18:01,163 --> 00:18:02,247
Oh no!

238
00:18:07,211 --> 00:18:12,466
I'm sorry, but I can't eat right now.

239
00:18:12,549 --> 00:18:16,136
The Ardientes invited me over
for breakfast.

240
00:18:17,846 --> 00:18:19,348
I'm excited to see them.

241
00:18:20,140 --> 00:18:22,392
I'm excited to see the look on their faces

242
00:18:22,476 --> 00:18:27,439
once they find out
Julio's statue was destroyed.

243
00:18:29,191 --> 00:18:31,944
I can't wait to see
the look on their faces.

244
00:18:35,864 --> 00:18:38,534
-I'll go get ready.
-Go ahead, dear.

245
00:18:54,007 --> 00:18:56,593
[utensils clanking]

246
00:18:59,179 --> 00:19:00,430
How's your arm, Governor?

247
00:19:02,099 --> 00:19:03,058
It's better now.

248
00:19:03,142 --> 00:19:06,270
I applied imported
burn ointment cream on it.

249
00:19:06,353 --> 00:19:07,604
I'm fine now.

250
00:19:07,688 --> 00:19:09,148
-That's good to hear.
-Mm-hm.

251
00:19:13,235 --> 00:19:16,321
Uh, aren't we short two people?

252
00:19:19,908 --> 00:19:25,164
Oh, Raul is in a nearby town,
managing our business there.

253
00:19:25,247 --> 00:19:29,084
Diego, on the other hand,
is with the farmers.

254
00:19:29,168 --> 00:19:31,503
-Diego's with the farmers?
-[Emilia] Yes.

255
00:19:31,587 --> 00:19:33,255
He must be close to them.

256
00:19:33,338 --> 00:19:37,426
So, why didn't he enter politics,
like Arnaldo?

257
00:19:37,509 --> 00:19:38,760
[gentle music playing]

258
00:19:39,386 --> 00:19:40,679
[chuckles]

259
00:19:40,762 --> 00:19:42,514
Let's just say

260
00:19:43,182 --> 00:19:47,686
Diego is not equipped
or suited for politics.

261
00:19:49,730 --> 00:19:52,816
Really, Congressman?
If he's close to the farmers,

262
00:19:52,900 --> 00:19:57,946
that means Diego can sympathize
with the less fortunate.

263
00:19:58,780 --> 00:20:01,992
Well,
let's look at it this way.

264
00:20:02,743 --> 00:20:06,872
Diego doesn't have the stomach
to make hard and difficult decisions.

265
00:20:07,831 --> 00:20:09,791
You know, Ivy, in politics,

266
00:20:09,875 --> 00:20:12,252
sympathizing with people isn't enough.

267
00:20:12,336 --> 00:20:14,296
You have to be tough
most of the time.

268
00:20:16,882 --> 00:20:18,258
Well, anyway.

269
00:20:18,342 --> 00:20:20,344
Let's not talk about people
who aren't here.

270
00:20:20,427 --> 00:20:22,471
Let's talk about the future.

271
00:20:22,554 --> 00:20:25,724
The bright future.
Your future here, in Ardiente.

272
00:20:25,807 --> 00:20:27,976
Like your investment.

273
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:29,603
We can talk about that.

274
00:20:29,686 --> 00:20:31,104
[man] Excuse me, Gov.

275
00:20:31,188 --> 00:20:34,107
Chief is outside.
He wants to see Congressman.

276
00:20:34,191 --> 00:20:36,443
Can you please tell him
to wait? Papa's still eating.

277
00:20:36,526 --> 00:20:38,445
Gov, it's very important.

278
00:20:40,239 --> 00:20:42,407
Fine, let him in.

279
00:20:43,909 --> 00:20:46,745
[tense music playing]

280
00:20:48,205 --> 00:20:49,122
[Julio] Well.

281
00:20:51,959 --> 00:20:54,670
Good morning, Gov,
Mayor, Congressman.

282
00:20:54,753 --> 00:20:56,129
[Julio] Good morning.

283
00:20:58,465 --> 00:21:03,095
It's okay, she's our guest.
Just tell us whatever you have to say.

284
00:21:04,054 --> 00:21:07,724
Uh, Congressman. Your statue at the plaza…

285
00:21:08,308 --> 00:21:09,559
[tense drum beat]

286
00:21:11,103 --> 00:21:12,271
…it was destroyed.

287
00:21:12,354 --> 00:21:16,275
-Papa? Who did this?
-How did that happen?

288
00:21:16,358 --> 00:21:17,943
Oh no, Papa.
This is really bad.

289
00:21:18,026 --> 00:21:20,529
This is not good, Papa!

290
00:21:21,238 --> 00:21:23,573
[Julio groans] Um…

291
00:21:23,657 --> 00:21:26,952
Arnaldo. Arnaldo, take me to the plaza.

292
00:21:27,035 --> 00:21:30,580
I want to see what happened to my statue.

293
00:21:30,664 --> 00:21:31,915
Yes, Grandpa.

294
00:21:31,999 --> 00:21:33,458
Miss Aguas, I'm sorry.

295
00:21:34,251 --> 00:21:36,044
I will have to leave you
in the hands of Emilia.

296
00:21:39,840 --> 00:21:40,882
I understand, Congressman.

297
00:21:40,966 --> 00:21:43,135
-Thank you.
-[Ivy] I hope everything's okay.

298
00:21:44,970 --> 00:21:46,513
Governor.

299
00:21:46,596 --> 00:21:48,015
This is not happening.

300
00:21:48,682 --> 00:21:52,060
Nanny,
get my cigarettes! Hurry!

301
00:21:52,144 --> 00:21:53,270
Gov, relax.

302
00:21:53,353 --> 00:21:55,522
This is not happening.

303
00:21:56,189 --> 00:21:57,316
[Emilia sighs]

304
00:21:58,525 --> 00:22:00,402
[cans clanking]

305
00:22:00,485 --> 00:22:02,904
[Arthur panting]

306
00:22:05,157 --> 00:22:07,242
[cans clanking]

307
00:22:07,326 --> 00:22:09,661
[shouting] It's here!

308
00:22:10,912 --> 00:22:13,874
The day has finally arrived!

309
00:22:14,374 --> 00:22:17,002
The entire town will be destroyed!

310
00:22:17,711 --> 00:22:22,132
Everyone who worships
that statue will be punished!

311
00:22:22,758 --> 00:22:25,093
[Arthur laughing]

312
00:22:29,222 --> 00:22:30,974
We're in trouble with Mayor
and Congressman.

313
00:22:31,058 --> 00:22:34,352
They're going to call us
incompetent again.

314
00:22:35,270 --> 00:22:38,815
"As long as this statue
stands in our town,

315
00:22:38,899 --> 00:22:41,359
you'll have honest service."

316
00:22:41,443 --> 00:22:43,612
[laughs]

317
00:22:43,695 --> 00:22:45,614
But it broke!

318
00:22:47,449 --> 00:22:49,659
If we could just pin it all
on that nutjob, it'd be over.

319
00:22:49,743 --> 00:22:50,660
[Arthur] It broke!

320
00:22:54,081 --> 00:22:57,084
[tense music playing]

321
00:23:22,609 --> 00:23:25,153
[heavy breathing]

322
00:23:31,034 --> 00:23:33,912
Someone wants to bring us down.

323
00:23:35,747 --> 00:23:39,584
Someone with the nerve
to do it this publicly.

324
00:23:41,211 --> 00:23:44,714
I'll make sure to capture
and punish whoever did this.

325
00:23:45,632 --> 00:23:47,092
They're utterly disrespectful.

326
00:23:47,175 --> 00:23:51,596
Our people must not assume
that we're getting weak.

327
00:23:54,850 --> 00:23:56,560
Any updates? Have you found a lead?

328
00:23:56,643 --> 00:23:59,688
I'm sorry, Mayor.
We didn't find any evidence.

329
00:24:00,355 --> 00:24:03,316
All we have is this surveillance footage.

330
00:24:07,445 --> 00:24:08,822
Arnaldo.

331
00:24:10,073 --> 00:24:10,991
Take it.

332
00:24:19,040 --> 00:24:20,876
Seal off the whole plaza.

333
00:24:20,959 --> 00:24:27,215
When I return,
I want my statue rebuilt again.

334
00:24:28,133 --> 00:24:29,634
Yes, Grandpa.

335
00:24:32,888 --> 00:24:35,348
[ominous music playing]

336
00:24:49,446 --> 00:24:51,990
Gov, don't worry.

337
00:24:52,073 --> 00:24:54,868
I'm sure Congressman will fix everything.

338
00:24:54,951 --> 00:24:58,455
After all,
this is Poblacion Ardiente.

339
00:24:58,538 --> 00:25:00,332
Zero crime rate ever since--

340
00:25:00,415 --> 00:25:01,917
Forever.

341
00:25:04,085 --> 00:25:07,339
But honestly, I'm scared
for the person who did this.

342
00:25:08,298 --> 00:25:10,550
For sure, they'll be punished in no time.

343
00:25:10,634 --> 00:25:12,719
You know that I don't want
my people getting hurt.

344
00:25:14,054 --> 00:25:17,682
I can't help but wonder.
Who would do such a thing?

345
00:25:17,766 --> 00:25:19,976
[tense music playing]

346
00:25:24,564 --> 00:25:25,899
Who else…

347
00:25:28,109 --> 00:25:30,278
but our rivals in politics.

348
00:25:32,781 --> 00:25:37,035
That's exactly why it's hard
to trust anyone these days.

349
00:25:40,747 --> 00:25:42,916
Anyway, I have to go now.

350
00:25:42,999 --> 00:25:44,793
If you need anything,
just call me.

351
00:25:45,919 --> 00:25:47,128
Thank you, Ivy.

352
00:25:48,338 --> 00:25:51,466
You're really a true friend,
not just to me but the whole Ardiente.

353
00:25:52,676 --> 00:25:53,718
Thank you.

354
00:25:54,886 --> 00:25:57,305
It feels so good

355
00:25:57,389 --> 00:26:00,308
to be considered a friend by the governor.

356
00:26:00,392 --> 00:26:03,061
-Thank you, Gov.
-Bye.

357
00:26:04,854 --> 00:26:06,064
Bye.

358
00:26:06,982 --> 00:26:08,441
Take care, okay?

359
00:26:13,154 --> 00:26:14,239
[car engine starts]

360
00:26:15,240 --> 00:26:17,117
-Bye!
-Take care.

361
00:26:21,121 --> 00:26:23,331
[tense music playing]

362
00:26:30,588 --> 00:26:33,466
We can now identify the bastard
who wants to ruin us.

363
00:26:38,888 --> 00:26:42,058
[tense music playing]

364
00:26:50,025 --> 00:26:51,651
-Huh?
-What happened?

365
00:26:52,944 --> 00:26:55,405
Why did the footage disappear?

366
00:26:56,656 --> 00:27:00,827
Perhaps someone switched it off
on purpose.

367
00:27:00,910 --> 00:27:04,080
[brooding music playing]

368
00:27:12,255 --> 00:27:13,423
I took care of everything.

369
00:27:16,593 --> 00:27:18,219
I understand why you did it.

370
00:27:19,429 --> 00:27:23,058
If it were me, I would've done
something much worse.

371
00:27:25,060 --> 00:27:26,519
Jepoy, thank you.

372
00:27:29,439 --> 00:27:31,483
You're always there to help me.

373
00:27:33,902 --> 00:27:35,111
And to catch me when I fall.

374
00:27:36,946 --> 00:27:38,448
[sighs deeply]

375
00:27:43,495 --> 00:27:45,038
For you…

376
00:27:47,040 --> 00:27:48,375
I'll do anything.

377
00:27:48,458 --> 00:27:51,628
[brooding music playing]

378
00:28:09,354 --> 00:28:10,814
[water splashes]

379
00:28:17,946 --> 00:28:21,991
I hate feeling like we're
being played by our enemies.

380
00:28:24,786 --> 00:28:27,872
We have to get to the bottom
of this as soon as possible.

381
00:28:28,498 --> 00:28:29,707
Do you understand?

382
00:28:34,087 --> 00:28:35,463
[sighs]

383
00:28:39,426 --> 00:28:42,429
[instrumental theme music playing]

384
00:29:00,739 --> 00:29:03,032
[Dante] <i>"Time flies so fast, doesn't it?</i>

385
00:29:03,533 --> 00:29:05,034
<i>It feels like just yesterday</i>

386
00:29:05,118 --> 00:29:08,246
<i>when I cried as I first held you.</i>

387
00:29:10,790 --> 00:29:14,544
<i>Do you remember the day</i>
<i>I taught you how to ride a bike?</i>

388
00:29:14,627 --> 00:29:18,423
<i>You fell a lot, but you kept getting up.</i>

389
00:29:19,340 --> 00:29:22,302
<i>You're a very strong and determined girl.</i>

390
00:29:24,804 --> 00:29:30,393
<i>In the near future,</i>
<i>thank yourself for those traits."</i>

391
00:29:30,477 --> 00:29:33,480
[instrumental theme music playing]

392
00:29:51,581 --> 00:29:54,417
First, my failed
assassination, and now this.

393
00:29:54,501 --> 00:29:57,504
Papa! These attacks worry me.

394
00:29:58,254 --> 00:30:00,507
What are our enemies up to?

395
00:30:00,590 --> 00:30:02,634
[tense music]

396
00:30:02,717 --> 00:30:04,135
Where is Raul?

397
00:30:06,888 --> 00:30:07,889
[Raul] Auntie.

398
00:30:08,598 --> 00:30:10,558
No need for you to stand up. Sit down.

399
00:30:10,642 --> 00:30:13,728
-[Belen] You're back so soon.
-Yeah.

400
00:30:13,812 --> 00:30:15,897
Why? Did something happen? Anything new?

401
00:30:15,980 --> 00:30:20,568
Just the usual. I didn't think
you'd be back right away.

402
00:30:20,652 --> 00:30:22,862
I don't plan on staying long.

403
00:30:23,738 --> 00:30:26,199
All they know is I had
some errands to run.

404
00:30:26,282 --> 00:30:29,244
It's good you haven't run out
of excuses to come here.

405
00:30:29,327 --> 00:30:31,079
I haven't.

406
00:30:31,162 --> 00:30:32,497
-Coffee?
-No, thanks.

407
00:30:32,580 --> 00:30:34,040
I'll just check on our friend.

408
00:30:34,123 --> 00:30:36,417
-Okay, go right in.
-Thanks.

409
00:30:38,670 --> 00:30:42,632
Whenever something happens, he's not here.

410
00:30:44,092 --> 00:30:45,552
Papa,
don't tell me you think Raul--

411
00:30:45,635 --> 00:30:47,470
Don't be stupid, Emilia.

412
00:30:48,721 --> 00:30:51,391
Your husband
is a coward and a weakling.

413
00:30:52,433 --> 00:30:55,854
If his disgraced father hadn't saved me,

414
00:30:55,937 --> 00:30:57,856
I would have silenced that idiot long ago.

415
00:30:57,939 --> 00:31:00,900
-Papa!
-No matter. Forget it. Forget it.

416
00:31:01,609 --> 00:31:04,487
It's better for him to busy himself
with the operations

417
00:31:04,571 --> 00:31:06,072
of our main source of income.

418
00:31:06,990 --> 00:31:09,868
Money has to keep coming in.

419
00:31:10,368 --> 00:31:12,161
[tense music]

420
00:31:19,586 --> 00:31:21,170
<i>Thirty-eight million.</i>

421
00:31:21,254 --> 00:31:23,631
[Joan]
Sold to our dear Mr. Senator.

422
00:31:23,715 --> 00:31:25,425
[Pablo]
Julio and I are good friends.

423
00:31:25,508 --> 00:31:28,219
He helped me win in the last elections.

424
00:31:28,303 --> 00:31:29,929
It's my turn to help him.

425
00:31:30,013 --> 00:31:31,973
[action music playing]

426
00:31:49,282 --> 00:31:52,535
SENATOR PABLO ALCANTARA
PASSES ANTI-JUETENG BILL

427
00:31:56,789 --> 00:31:58,082
[Emilia] <i>Don't worry, Papa.</i>

428
00:31:58,166 --> 00:32:01,044
I'll add more men around
the premises to protect us.

429
00:32:01,836 --> 00:32:04,380
You mean additional security?

430
00:32:04,881 --> 00:32:06,424
Are you
out of your mind, Emilia?

431
00:32:06,507 --> 00:32:09,385
Do you want us to look like
cowards and idiots

432
00:32:09,469 --> 00:32:10,595
in the eyes of our enemies?

433
00:32:12,847 --> 00:32:14,557
-That's not what I meant--
-Shut up!

434
00:32:15,350 --> 00:32:17,435
Let the men handle this.

435
00:32:18,019 --> 00:32:20,355
A woman like you wouldn't
understand anything.

436
00:32:21,022 --> 00:32:23,274
Sorry, Papa.
I was just suggesting.

437
00:32:23,358 --> 00:32:26,945
We are not going to give
our enemies the satisfaction

438
00:32:27,612 --> 00:32:29,822
of seeing us running scared.

439
00:32:29,906 --> 00:32:32,825
We will handle this but discreetly.

440
00:32:34,369 --> 00:32:35,578
Arnaldo.

441
00:32:36,621 --> 00:32:40,375
Monitor
who goes in and out of town.

442
00:32:40,458 --> 00:32:45,213
Get a list of all the names
of those visiting Poblacion Ardiente.

443
00:32:46,005 --> 00:32:49,092
From the very day of the attempted
assassination on your mother.

444
00:32:49,175 --> 00:32:52,595
And do
a background check on all of them.

445
00:32:54,138 --> 00:32:56,683
Oh. Papa,
does this include Ivy?

446
00:32:59,477 --> 00:33:01,854
Especially Ivy.

447
00:33:02,522 --> 00:33:06,234
I know we did
a background check on her already, but…

448
00:33:07,235 --> 00:33:10,989
these things started
the moment she came here.

449
00:33:12,156 --> 00:33:14,242
But Papa, she saved my life.

450
00:33:14,325 --> 00:33:15,785
She even
invested in our project,

451
00:33:15,868 --> 00:33:19,789
so why would we assume she's against us?

452
00:33:21,249 --> 00:33:24,335
Have you really learned
nothing at all, Emilia?

453
00:33:25,003 --> 00:33:30,383
In the world of politics,
any of your allies

454
00:33:30,466 --> 00:33:33,594
can sometimes be your greatest enemy.

455
00:33:34,804 --> 00:33:37,807
Must I keep drilling that into your head?

456
00:33:38,516 --> 00:33:40,309
I'll handle Ivy, Papa.

457
00:33:40,393 --> 00:33:42,854
I'll uncover
her deepest secrets.

458
00:33:43,688 --> 00:33:45,648
Don't fail me, Emilia.

459
00:33:46,315 --> 00:33:49,736
[ominous music playing]

460
00:33:54,782 --> 00:33:58,536
-[Loring] Here. Here.
-[Pandoy] Everyone, let's eat! Come on.

461
00:33:59,328 --> 00:34:00,997
-Did that tire you, son?
-It's good.

462
00:34:01,080 --> 00:34:02,623
-[man] Here we go.
-Wow, banana fritters!

463
00:34:02,707 --> 00:34:03,875
[townsfolk cheering]

464
00:34:03,958 --> 00:34:05,877
[Fernan] Come dig in!
Don't be shy. Go get some.

465
00:34:05,960 --> 00:34:06,919
-Fritters!
-[Fernan] Use your hands.

466
00:34:07,003 --> 00:34:10,590
[Fernan] Our harvest
has been fruitful! We got lucky!

467
00:34:11,174 --> 00:34:14,469
Mister Fernan, let's not forget
to thank Diego

468
00:34:14,552 --> 00:34:16,804
for teaching us
the new technologies in farming.

469
00:34:16,888 --> 00:34:18,556
We reaped so much!

470
00:34:18,639 --> 00:34:21,142
-That's right.
-[all chanting] Diego!

471
00:34:21,225 --> 00:34:23,853
[chanting] Diego!

472
00:34:23,936 --> 00:34:25,772
Thank you. Thank you, everyone.

473
00:34:26,397 --> 00:34:28,608
I'm happy with our harvest this year too.

474
00:34:30,651 --> 00:34:31,652
But…

475
00:34:32,612 --> 00:34:36,407
we have a huge problem.
I was at the party last night.

476
00:34:37,408 --> 00:34:39,035
And I found out that…

477
00:34:39,619 --> 00:34:41,329
the project will push through here.

478
00:34:42,121 --> 00:34:43,206
It's good to hear the mayor

479
00:34:43,289 --> 00:34:45,458
and congressman's project
will push through.

480
00:34:45,541 --> 00:34:47,794
I'm sure it'll be beneficial to all of us.

481
00:34:47,877 --> 00:34:49,921
Are you serious? That's not true!

482
00:34:50,004 --> 00:34:51,089
If the project happens,

483
00:34:51,172 --> 00:34:53,382
most of our land and even
this cooperative will disappear!

484
00:34:53,466 --> 00:34:54,675
Come on!

485
00:34:54,759 --> 00:34:57,011
We'll have to move? That's not right!

486
00:34:57,095 --> 00:34:58,554
We've been cultivating this land
for so long.

487
00:34:58,638 --> 00:35:00,139
Do they think we'll leave so easily?

488
00:35:00,223 --> 00:35:02,517
-[townsfolk] He's right.
-[man] Mr. Diego, what's this about?

489
00:35:02,600 --> 00:35:04,560
Diego, is it true they'll force us out?

490
00:35:04,644 --> 00:35:05,770
[man] Sir?

491
00:35:05,853 --> 00:35:08,731
We'll find a way so none of you
will get affected.

492
00:35:08,815 --> 00:35:12,026
I will make sure your complaints
will reach the congressman.

493
00:35:12,110 --> 00:35:14,695
We'll send a formal complaint
to his office.

494
00:35:14,779 --> 00:35:17,365
-Thank you, Mr. Diego.
-Thank you.

495
00:35:17,448 --> 00:35:19,617
[man] We're counting on you, sir.

496
00:35:21,369 --> 00:35:23,871
[Joan] Miss Aguas, I'll just inform you

497
00:35:23,955 --> 00:35:26,415
once we finalize the date
and the time of the conference call.

498
00:35:26,499 --> 00:35:28,292
Okay, Joan. Thank you.

499
00:35:31,629 --> 00:35:34,006
[Emilia] Yes, I'm on my way.

500
00:35:34,090 --> 00:35:36,759
I'll just drop by Miss Aguas' place.

501
00:35:36,843 --> 00:35:39,137
Okay, bye.

502
00:35:39,220 --> 00:35:41,430
[pensive music playing]

503
00:35:48,354 --> 00:35:50,022
[phone ringing]

504
00:35:53,943 --> 00:35:55,278
Yes, Jepoy?

505
00:35:55,361 --> 00:35:57,488
Hello, Ivy? Emilia's on her way there.

506
00:35:57,572 --> 00:36:00,074
[tense music playing]

507
00:36:00,700 --> 00:36:01,909
Really?

508
00:36:03,035 --> 00:36:06,330
No worries. I've prepared for her arrival.

509
00:36:16,841 --> 00:36:17,800
-Sweetie?
-Nanny.

510
00:36:17,884 --> 00:36:21,554
-I'll go buy groceries, okay?
-All right. Stay safe, okay?

511
00:36:22,471 --> 00:36:25,266
Oh, I do have a favor to ask.

512
00:36:25,349 --> 00:36:27,143
Remember that blabbermouth at the market?

513
00:36:27,852 --> 00:36:29,145
Can you talk to her?

514
00:36:29,228 --> 00:36:32,231
Just ask her about what happened
to Julio's statue.

515
00:36:33,941 --> 00:36:35,860
All right, dear. You can count on me.

516
00:36:35,943 --> 00:36:38,321
-Thank you. Take care.
-You too.

517
00:36:38,821 --> 00:36:41,824
[tense music playing]

518
00:36:48,414 --> 00:36:51,417
[dramatic music]

519
00:36:52,668 --> 00:36:53,961
Ma'am.

520
00:36:54,503 --> 00:36:56,422
Ivy.

521
00:36:56,505 --> 00:36:59,842
Governor?
Governor, what a surprise!

522
00:36:59,926 --> 00:37:01,802
We were
just together a while ago.

523
00:37:01,886 --> 00:37:03,596
[Emilia] Hi!

524
00:37:03,679 --> 00:37:07,600
Juice or, I know it's still
early, but champagne maybe?

525
00:37:07,683 --> 00:37:09,894
No, I'm fine.
I'll pass this time.

526
00:37:09,977 --> 00:37:11,354
I still
need to go to the town hall.

527
00:37:11,437 --> 00:37:13,022
I came here to deliver this.

528
00:37:13,105 --> 00:37:16,108
[light music playing]

529
00:37:20,071 --> 00:37:21,864
Governor, I'm a little worried.

530
00:37:21,948 --> 00:37:25,034
This morning, my helpers
went to the market

531
00:37:25,534 --> 00:37:27,787
and told me what happened
to Congressman's statue

532
00:37:27,870 --> 00:37:29,872
is the talk of the town.

533
00:37:29,956 --> 00:37:31,624
[chuckles]

534
00:37:31,707 --> 00:37:34,585
I guess it's true what they say,
that news travels fast.

535
00:37:34,669 --> 00:37:36,128
And the market

536
00:37:36,212 --> 00:37:40,007
is the breeding ground of flies,
rats, and rumors!

537
00:37:40,091 --> 00:37:41,092
[scoffs]

538
00:37:41,175 --> 00:37:43,928
Don't worry, Ivy.
We are doing something about it.

539
00:37:44,011 --> 00:37:47,181
As we speak, the people
behind it are being apprehended.

540
00:37:49,850 --> 00:37:53,187
But everything that's
been happening got me thinking.

541
00:37:53,271 --> 00:37:54,981
It's bothering me.

542
00:37:56,983 --> 00:37:58,442
What do you mean?

543
00:38:00,194 --> 00:38:05,157
Governor, now that someone's openly
going against you, it's troubling.

544
00:38:05,825 --> 00:38:07,743
I'm starting
to reconsider my investment.

545
00:38:10,288 --> 00:38:13,082
-[Diego] Can you load these on the truck?
-[man] Yes, sir!

546
00:38:13,165 --> 00:38:15,459
[indistinct chatter]

547
00:38:22,758 --> 00:38:24,427
Wait!

548
00:38:24,510 --> 00:38:27,638
Why does everyone look so dull?
Come on, guys.

549
00:38:28,431 --> 00:38:32,435
Can we forget about our problem
with the land for a while?

550
00:38:32,518 --> 00:38:34,353
Let's enjoy our amazing harvest!

551
00:38:35,354 --> 00:38:39,817
Why don't we have a feast tomorrow?

552
00:38:39,900 --> 00:38:42,820
Yes! Let's do that! That's a great idea!

553
00:38:42,903 --> 00:38:49,577
I'll cook some banana fritters
for dessert tomorrow.

554
00:38:49,660 --> 00:38:51,454
But you have to pay
for what you ate today.

555
00:38:51,537 --> 00:38:54,874
-Miss Loring, come on!
-[Loring] Just kidding!

556
00:38:54,957 --> 00:38:55,958
-I thought…
-That's great!

557
00:38:56,042 --> 00:38:58,711
We're like a family here.

558
00:38:58,794 --> 00:39:00,171
We might have our differences,

559
00:39:00,254 --> 00:39:03,841
but we all agree when it comes
to our land and harvest.

560
00:39:03,924 --> 00:39:05,426
-That's true.
-That's right, boss.

561
00:39:05,509 --> 00:39:07,720
This is where I get money
to send my son to school.

562
00:39:07,803 --> 00:39:10,765
And this is the only way
I can afford my mother's medicine.

563
00:39:10,848 --> 00:39:13,517
This is for my son's school allowance.

564
00:39:13,601 --> 00:39:18,147
See that? All of us depend on this land.

565
00:39:18,230 --> 00:39:19,774
So, if it'll be taken from us

566
00:39:19,857 --> 00:39:23,736
just because
of that new project, what then?

567
00:39:23,819 --> 00:39:25,363
-That's right.
-Right.

568
00:39:25,446 --> 00:39:27,406
-Exactly.
-Wait.

569
00:39:28,783 --> 00:39:32,203
Write in here all you
want to say to the congressman.

570
00:39:32,286 --> 00:39:36,999
I promise you
I'll deliver it to him myself.

571
00:39:37,083 --> 00:39:40,294
-Boss, can I go first?
-Sure.

572
00:39:40,378 --> 00:39:41,295
-Everyone!
-What happened, Cora?

573
00:39:41,379 --> 00:39:42,797
-Ms. Loring.
-What took you so long?

574
00:39:42,880 --> 00:39:44,131
And why are you out of breath?

575
00:39:45,299 --> 00:39:46,801
There's news going around town.

576
00:39:46,884 --> 00:39:47,927
What news?

577
00:39:48,010 --> 00:39:51,013
The congressman's statue
was destroyed last night!

578
00:39:51,097 --> 00:39:52,306
-What?
-That's right.

579
00:39:52,390 --> 00:39:54,433
[woman] Who could've done it?

580
00:39:54,517 --> 00:39:57,103
Come on, Ivy.
I thought we're friends!

581
00:39:57,186 --> 00:39:59,814
Of course, we are!

582
00:39:59,897 --> 00:40:02,066
But this is different.
This is business!

583
00:40:03,692 --> 00:40:05,194
Yes, I understand.

584
00:40:05,277 --> 00:40:08,447
But you know
I won't let you do that, right?

585
00:40:09,240 --> 00:40:10,616
You know why?

586
00:40:10,699 --> 00:40:12,159
Because we're friends!

587
00:40:12,243 --> 00:40:13,494
I want you to earn well,

588
00:40:13,577 --> 00:40:15,704
which won't happen
if you pull out of your investment.

589
00:40:15,788 --> 00:40:18,082
Governor, I don't need to earn money.

590
00:40:18,165 --> 00:40:19,750
I'm already rich, remember?

591
00:40:19,834 --> 00:40:21,710
I can buy anything I want.

592
00:40:21,794 --> 00:40:25,798
What matters to me is I protect
my reputation and my company.

593
00:40:26,841 --> 00:40:28,300
I don't want to get involved
with any issues.

594
00:40:28,384 --> 00:40:32,513
And since you're in politics,
I'm sure you understand me.

595
00:40:33,973 --> 00:40:37,143
Of course, Ivy.
I completely understand.

596
00:40:37,226 --> 00:40:40,813
But you know, once you're in bed
with an Ardiente,

597
00:40:40,896 --> 00:40:42,982
you can't just easily back out.

598
00:40:43,065 --> 00:40:47,611
And after all, we publicly
announced our partnership.

599
00:40:48,112 --> 00:40:50,698
You wouldn't want to
humiliate a friend, right?

600
00:40:51,449 --> 00:40:55,369
And a true friend
never backs out on a promise.

601
00:40:55,453 --> 00:40:57,079
But I haven't promised anything yet.

602
00:40:59,498 --> 00:41:02,877
I mean, I haven't signed
any contracts yet.

603
00:41:03,961 --> 00:41:05,629
Is that it? Don't worry.

604
00:41:05,713 --> 00:41:08,591
I'll have the papers ready
by tomorrow, so you can sign them.

605
00:41:08,674 --> 00:41:10,050
But it's not that easy, Governor.

606
00:41:10,134 --> 00:41:12,052
Of course, my lawyers
still need to check it.

607
00:41:12,136 --> 00:41:15,514
And if they're okay with it,
then we won't have a problem.

608
00:41:16,474 --> 00:41:17,808
Of course!

609
00:41:18,517 --> 00:41:19,685
Anyway, I have to go.

610
00:41:19,768 --> 00:41:21,812
I need
to head to the town hall.

611
00:41:21,896 --> 00:41:23,814
You know,
my constituents are waiting.

612
00:41:26,484 --> 00:41:27,610
Thank you.

613
00:41:28,694 --> 00:41:30,696
-Governor.
-Yes?

614
00:41:31,405 --> 00:41:36,368
As your friend,
I want you to be extra careful.

615
00:41:36,452 --> 00:41:38,662
I'm sure your enemies
are watching your every move.

616
00:41:41,040 --> 00:41:42,708
Oh no, sweetheart.

617
00:41:42,791 --> 00:41:44,835
I don't need to be careful.

618
00:41:45,336 --> 00:41:47,463
They're the ones who have to be.

619
00:41:47,546 --> 00:41:48,672
Bye!

620
00:41:48,756 --> 00:41:51,383
[somber music playing]

621
00:41:58,057 --> 00:42:00,559
[dramatic music playing]

622
00:42:04,855 --> 00:42:05,773
[gun cocks]

623
00:42:11,654 --> 00:42:14,240
[gunshots ring out]

624
00:42:17,618 --> 00:42:22,873
Whoever you are going against
my family, I'll make you suffer.

625
00:42:23,499 --> 00:42:24,833
You'll pay for this.

626
00:42:28,629 --> 00:42:30,297
[gunshot rings out]

627
00:42:35,928 --> 00:42:38,430
[panting]

628
00:42:40,432 --> 00:42:44,144
I'll deploy my elite team
to watch over our checkpoints.

629
00:42:44,895 --> 00:42:47,565
I don't want
just your elite team, Superintendent.

630
00:42:48,190 --> 00:42:53,195
I would suggest getting officers
from the provincial headquarters too.

631
00:42:53,279 --> 00:42:57,575
After the tampering
with the security footage from the plaza,

632
00:42:58,367 --> 00:43:01,161
I've lost my trust
in the police force in our town.

633
00:43:02,663 --> 00:43:03,956
Noted, Congressman.

634
00:43:04,707 --> 00:43:06,000
Thank you, Superintendent.

635
00:43:07,501 --> 00:43:08,627
You may go.

636
00:43:12,464 --> 00:43:13,549
Good morning, ma'am.

637
00:43:14,967 --> 00:43:16,927
Papa, look at this.

638
00:43:19,555 --> 00:43:22,099
Oh. Why do you have this?

639
00:43:23,100 --> 00:43:23,934
Papa.

640
00:43:24,018 --> 00:43:27,563
I have to lock down
the deal with Ivy as soon as possible.

641
00:43:27,646 --> 00:43:29,315
Before she changes her mind.

642
00:43:29,398 --> 00:43:31,025
She knows what's happening.

643
00:43:31,108 --> 00:43:34,486
Wait. What did you do
to make her back out?

644
00:43:34,570 --> 00:43:36,697
I didn't do anything, Papa.

645
00:43:36,780 --> 00:43:38,616
Don't be a liar, Emilia.

646
00:43:38,699 --> 00:43:42,411
You must've done something
for her to change her mind.

647
00:43:42,494 --> 00:43:45,581
You're such a worthless person!

648
00:43:45,664 --> 00:43:48,459
-That's so unfair, Papa.
-Shut up.

649
00:43:49,209 --> 00:43:50,628
We have to fix this.

650
00:43:50,711 --> 00:43:55,007
We need that woman and her money.

651
00:43:57,343 --> 00:43:58,636
Yes, Papa.

652
00:44:00,304 --> 00:44:01,639
Emilia.

653
00:44:02,139 --> 00:44:04,224
Please,
don't do anything anymore.

654
00:44:04,892 --> 00:44:07,311
Talk to Arnaldo.

655
00:44:07,394 --> 00:44:09,563
He can handle this
better than you.

656
00:44:12,316 --> 00:44:15,110
Arnaldo knows
how to charm that woman.

657
00:44:16,779 --> 00:44:17,780
Go.

658
00:44:18,947 --> 00:44:20,991
[tense music playing]

659
00:44:28,874 --> 00:44:30,793
You'll go down, Ardientes.

660
00:44:32,461 --> 00:44:33,962
[Arthur giggling]

661
00:44:34,046 --> 00:44:36,215
-They're here. [laughs]
-Shh.

662
00:44:36,965 --> 00:44:40,052
Our savior has come to this town.

663
00:44:41,178 --> 00:44:42,221
They'll bring you down!

664
00:44:42,304 --> 00:44:43,347
[raspberry sound]

665
00:44:43,430 --> 00:44:45,557
-What did you say?
-Mayor. Mayor. Mayor!

666
00:44:46,266 --> 00:44:47,393
Hold on. I got this.

667
00:44:50,062 --> 00:44:52,648
[wicked laugh]

668
00:44:58,028 --> 00:45:00,697
I saw. I saw them.

669
00:45:00,781 --> 00:45:03,450
[suspenseful music playing]

670
00:45:03,534 --> 00:45:06,245
A woman

671
00:45:07,663 --> 00:45:09,039
and a man.

672
00:45:10,666 --> 00:45:14,586
They had a sledgehammer.
They destroyed the statue.

673
00:45:15,546 --> 00:45:17,673
[Arthur chuckling]

674
00:45:17,756 --> 00:45:20,008
-I saw them!
-Uh…

675
00:45:20,092 --> 00:45:22,136
I saw them!

676
00:45:22,219 --> 00:45:24,304
-Wait! Where…
-Ardiente is going down!

677
00:45:25,889 --> 00:45:28,725
-Hey! Stop!
-Ardiente is going down!

678
00:45:28,809 --> 00:45:30,436
[Arthur laughing]

679
00:45:31,562 --> 00:45:34,690
Grandpa. I heard what happened.

680
00:45:34,773 --> 00:45:36,692
[tense music playing]

681
00:45:36,775 --> 00:45:39,486
It doesn't concern you, Diego.

682
00:45:39,570 --> 00:45:41,029
Stay out of this.

683
00:45:41,113 --> 00:45:42,781
But I'm worried about you.

684
00:45:45,242 --> 00:45:46,952
There's no need.

685
00:45:47,536 --> 00:45:51,331
This is the first and last time

686
00:45:52,082 --> 00:45:55,252
that I let anyone openly oppose me.

687
00:45:56,336 --> 00:45:59,339
[tense music playing]

688
00:46:03,385 --> 00:46:05,387
[Diego] <i>Don't try to fool the farmers.</i>

689
00:46:05,471 --> 00:46:07,347
<i>You're just after the land, right?</i>

690
00:46:07,431 --> 00:46:09,933
<i>You're smart enough to see that.</i>
<i>And you're beautiful too.</i>

691
00:46:10,017 --> 00:46:12,436
<i>It's a shame you don't have a good heart.</i>

692
00:46:12,519 --> 00:46:14,855
<i>You're giving me a hard time,</i>
<i>and I'm not liking it.</i>

693
00:46:14,938 --> 00:46:18,400
<i>If the congressman were the one asking me,</i>

694
00:46:18,484 --> 00:46:19,693
<i>I might say yes to him.</i>

695
00:46:19,776 --> 00:46:21,236
<i>You don't know what you're talking about.</i>

696
00:46:21,320 --> 00:46:22,988
<i>I can read you like a book,</i>
<i>Governor Emilia.</i>

697
00:46:23,071 --> 00:46:24,990
<i>From head to toe.</i>

698
00:46:25,073 --> 00:46:27,075
<i>Someone saw you destroying the statue.</i>

699
00:46:27,159 --> 00:46:29,578
-[Ivy] <i>What?</i>
-[Jepoy] <i>His name is Arthur. He's nuts.</i>

700
00:46:29,661 --> 00:46:31,038
<i>Who ordered you?</i>

701
00:46:31,788 --> 00:46:34,291
<i>I'll talk! I'll talk!</i>

702
00:46:34,374 --> 00:46:36,418
<i>I'll talk! I'll talk!</i>

703
00:46:36,502 --> 00:46:39,338
[theme music playing]
